message.content:
This is a Christmas decoration swag made of plastic, so it falls under festive articles in heading 9505. Artificial foliage of plastic would otherwise go to 6702, but Note 1 to Chapter 67 excludes festive articles. Heading 9505 covers "festive, carnival or other entertainment articles" and subheading 9505.10 covers Christmas articles. Within that, 9505.10.25 is "Other: Of plastics," and 9505.10.15 is "Glass articles." In the HTSUS, 9505.10.10 is nativity scenes, 9505.10.15 is glass, 9505.10.25 is "Other: Of plastics," and 9505.10.35 is of other materials. The 10-digit codes are 9505.10.2500 for plastics and 9505.10.5000 for others.

The swag is predominantly plastic, so it goes under 9505.10.25.00.

{"hts_code": "9505.10.2500", "reason": "A plastic artificial foliage swag marketed exclusively as a Christmas decoration is a festive article of plastics under heading 9505 (Christmas decorations), not artificial foliage of heading 6702."}
